 ## Background
-The method is described in "Anisotropic Ambient Volume Shading" [S1]. It builds on the concept of using geometry tensors (covariance matrices) to estimate local surface orientation and anisotropy in volumetric data. The approach avoids the high cost of on-the-fly curvature estimation by prefiltering and storing the necessary tensor data [S1].
